+# PIECES · summary card
+
+Goal: `npm run render` (from `src/card.mjs`) produces a 640 × 360 SVG that matches the deck's reference card; `npm run capture` writes `captures/card.svg` and `captures/CAPTURE.md`, which is what the critics judge. `npm test` must stay green throughout.
+
+The card has three real seams, one per source file, and the pieces follow them. Built in this order each piece can be judged on its own: the frame is a single top-level element before the groups, the header lives entirely in `<g id="header">`, the trend entirely in `<g id="trend">`. Nothing in a later piece is needed to judge an earlier one.
+
+Shared conventions every piece uses (copy them exactly; owners do not see the reference):
+
+- Canvas 640 × 360, `viewBox="0 0 640 360"`, `font-family="Inter, Helvetica, Arial, sans-serif"` on the `<svg>` (already there).
+- Margin 24 on every side: content spans x = 24 … 616 (inner width 592). Nothing touches an edge; nothing overlaps.
+- Palette, and nothing else: white `#ffffff` (card), hairline grey `#e5e7eb` (border, baseline line), tile grey `#f3f4f6`, ink `#1f2933` (titles and values), muted `#6b7280` (labels, period, month names), rise green `#1a7f37`, fall red `#c62828`, accent blue `#2f6fed` (bars), dark accent `#1b4fc1` (best month's bar only).
+- Small upper-case labels are the same everywhere: `font-size="11" font-weight="600" fill="#6b7280" letter-spacing="0.6"`, text in CAPITALS.
+- Every `<text>` carries an explicit `fill`; every colour is a 6-digit lower-case hex literal; no `<defs>`, gradients, filters, shadows, legend or gridlines.
+- Values are computed from `data/summary.json`, never hard-coded; the same code must work for any group's JSON of the same shape.
+
+---
+
+## Piece 1 · Card frame
+
+**Owner scope:** `src/card.mjs` only. Keep the exported `WIDTH`, `HEIGHT`, `renderCard(data)`, the `<svg …>` opening line as it is, and the two groups `<g id="header">…</g>` and `<g id="trend">…</g>` in that order. Do not touch `src/header.mjs`, `src/trend.mjs`, `scripts/`, `tests/`.
+
+**Reference cut:** the card is a white rounded panel with a hairline border, drawn once at top level, before the header group, so every later element sits on it.
+
+Exactly one element is added, as the first child of `<svg>`, on its own line:
+
+```svg
+<rect x="0.5" y="0.5" width="639" height="359" rx="12" fill="#ffffff" stroke="#e5e7eb"/>
+```
+
+- Position/size 0.5, 0.5, 639 × 359 (the half-pixel inset keeps the 1px stroke crisp inside the 640 × 360 canvas); corner radius 12; fill `#ffffff`; stroke `#e5e7eb`; no `stroke-width` attribute (defaults to 1).
+- Document order after this piece: `<svg>` line, the frame rect, `<g id="header">`, `<g id="trend">`, `</svg>`, trailing newline. The frame rect is the only element outside a group.
+- `npm run capture` must then describe the first element as: `(top level) · rect x=0.5 y=0.5 w=639 h=359 rx=12 fill=#ffffff stroke=#e5e7eb`.
+
+**Acceptance (critic checks `captures/CAPTURE.md` and `captures/card.svg` after `npm run capture`):**
+
+- The first listed element is exactly the top-level rect above (position, size, rx, fill, stroke); it is the only top-level element.
+- `<svg>` still declares 640 × 360 with the viewBox and font-family; groups `header` and `trend` follow in that order.
+- `npm test` passes.
+
+- [x] Piece 1 · Card frame
+
+---
+
+## Piece 2 · Header: title, period, three stat tiles
+
+**Owner scope:** `src/header.mjs` (rewrite freely; keep `export function renderHeader(data)` returning an SVG fragment string). May create `src/format.mjs` for shared number formatting (compact value, signed percentage) if that is cleaner; nothing else. Do not touch `src/card.mjs`, `src/trend.mjs`, `scripts/`, `tests/`.
+
+**Reference cut:** the header is a 20px semi-bold title at the top-left margin, a 12px muted period line under it, then one row of three equal grey tiles spanning the full inner width, each tile carrying a small upper-case label, a large bold compact value and a colour-signed change line, all on fixed baselines shared across the three tiles.
+
+Title and period (both at x = 24, no `text-anchor`):
+
+| element | x | y (baseline) | font-size | font-weight | fill | text |
+|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|
+| title | 24 | 40 | 20 | 600 | `#1f2933` | `data.title` → `Northwind Stores` |
+| period | 24 | 60 | 12 | (none) | `#6b7280` | `data.period` → `12 months to August 2026` |
+
+Tiles: one per entry in `data.stats`, in order, laid out left to right. Tile `i` (0-based):
+
+- Background: `<rect x="{24 + i*200}" y="84" width="192" height="96" rx="8" fill="#f3f4f6"/>` — so the three rects are at x = 24, 224, 424; widths 192; gap 8; the row runs exactly from 24 to 616. No stroke.
+- Text inside the tile is inset 16 from the tile's left edge: text x = `40 + i*200` (40, 240, 440). Three lines, on these baselines for every tile:
+  - **Label** y = 108, the shared small-label style (`font-size="11" font-weight="600" fill="#6b7280" letter-spacing="0.6"`), text = `stat.label` upper-cased: `REVENUE`, `ORDERS`, `AVG ORDER`.
+  - **Value** y = 146, `font-size="28" font-weight="700" fill="#1f2933"`, compact form (rules below): `$1.42M`, `38.2k`, `$37.24`.
+  - **Change** y = 166, `font-size="12" font-weight="600"`, fill and mark by sign (rules below): `▲ 12.4% vs prior period` (green), `▼ 3.1% vs prior period` (red), `▲ 15.8% vs prior period` (green).
+- Emit order per tile: rect, label, value, change; tiles in stats order. Header document order overall: title, period, tile 0 (4 elements), tile 1, tile 2 — 14 elements.
+
+Compact value formatting by `stat.unit` (derive from the number; do not hard-code the strings):
+
+- `usd`: dollars. ≥ 1,000,000 → `$` + value/1e6 to 2 decimals + `M` (1423000 → `$1.42M`); 1,000 … 999,999 → `$` + value/1e3 to 1 decimal + `k` (142300 → `$142.3k`); below 1,000 → `$` + integer.
+- `count`: ≥ 1,000,000 → 2 decimals + `M`; ≥ 1,000 → value/1e3 to 1 decimal + `k` (38210 → `38.2k`); below 1,000 → the integer.
+- `cents`: `$` + (value / 100) to exactly 2 decimals (3724 → `$37.24`).
+- Never the raw integer, never a thousands separator, never cents for revenue.
+
+Change line from `stat.delta` (a fraction): mark then a space then `|delta| × 100` to one decimal, `%`, then ` vs prior period`. delta ≥ 0 → `▲` (U+25B2) with `fill="#1a7f37"`; delta < 0 → `▼` (U+25BC) with `fill="#c62828"`. 0.124 → `▲ 12.4% vs prior period`; -0.031 → `▼ 3.1% vs prior period`; 0.158 → `▲ 15.8% vs prior period`. Write the arrow characters literally in the source (UTF-8), not as entities.
+
